      {
        "id": "lem-modified-patankar-euler-positive-tube-local-error-and-stability",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Modified Patankar Euler has a uniform first-order defect and one-step bound on positive tubes",
        "deps": [
          "alg-modified-patankar-euler",
          "def-finite-conservative-production-destruction-system",
          "lem-strict-column-dominance-implies-nonnegative-inverse",
          "def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution",
          "def-one-step-ode-method-local-defect-order-and-stability",
          "def-ck-and-multi-index-notation-in-several-variables",
          "thm-continuous-partial-derivatives-imply-total-differentiability",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "thm-chain-sum-product-and-composition-rules-for-banach-derivatives",
          "def-euclidean-inner-product",
          "def-induced-matrix-p-norm",
          "thm-induced-matrix-norms-are-compatible-submultiplicative-and-normalized",
          "thm-mean-value-inequality-for-total-derivatives",
          "thm-multivariable-taylor-formula-with-lagrange-remainder"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Let $F$ be the vector field of a finite conservative PDS [[def-finite-conservative-production-destruction-system]] on a bounded open convex set $U\\subset\\Omega\\cap\\mathbb R_{>0}^m$ with $\\overline U\\subset\\mathbb R_{>0}^m$. Suppose there is an open set $V$ with $\\overline U\\subset V\\subset\\Omega\\cap\\mathbb R_{>0}^m$ on which the transfer rates are multivariable $C^2$ and their derivatives through order two are bounded. For $y\\in U$, let $\\Phi_h(y)$ be [[alg-modified-patankar-euler]] with the standard denominators $\\sigma_i=y_i$. Then there are constants $C,L,h_0>0$ such that, for $0<h\\le h_0$:\n\n1. for every exact solution $y(t)$ whose segment and the method states under consideration remain in a compact subset of $U$, the exact-start local defect satisfies $\\|\\Phi_h(y(t))-y(t+h)\\|_2\\le Ch^2$; and\n2. for all $u,v\\in U$, $\\|\\Phi_h(u)-\\Phi_h(v)\\|_2\\le(1+Lh)\\|u-v\\|_2$.\n\nThe defect is the method output minus the exact next state and the second inequality is one-step Lipschitz stability in the convention of [[def-one-step-ode-method-local-defect-order-and-stability]]. This result is restricted to a compact positive tube; it does not define the standard ratio formula at zero compartments.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-zero-compatible-modified-patankar-euler-admissibility",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "The factorized zero-state step is well-defined, nonnegative, conservative, and locally first order",
        "deps": [
          "alg-zero-compatible-modified-patankar-euler",
          "def-source-factored-production-destruction-rates",
          "def-finite-conservative-production-destruction-system",
          "lem-strict-column-dominance-implies-nonnegative-inverse",
