        "title": "Certified residuals bound mass drift and the exact-solve positivity margin",
        "deps": [
          "alg-modified-patankar-euler",
          "alg-mprk22-1",
          "def-finite-conservative-production-destruction-system",
          "lem-strict-column-dominance-implies-nonnegative-inverse",
          "lem-rounded-linear-and-normal-residual-certificates",
          "def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma",
          "thm-cauchy-schwarz-and-the-euclidean-norm"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 3
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-mprk22-1-global-second-order-error",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "MPRK22(1) has global second-order error on a compact positive tube",
        "deps": [
          "alg-mprk22-1",
          "thm-mprk22-1-positive-conservative",
          "lem-mprk22-1-positive-tube-local-error-and-stability",
          "def-one-step-ode-method-local-defect-order-and-stability",
          "def-finite-conservative-production-destruction-system",
          "def-first-order-ode-initial-value-problem-and-solution",
          "def-euclidean-inner-product",
          "thm-global-error-from-one-step-defect-and-stability"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 4,
        "statement": "Let $T>0$, $N\\ge1$, $h=T/N$, and $t_n=nh$. Use sets $U,V$ satisfying the domain and regularity hypotheses of [[lem-mprk22-1-positive-tube-local-error-and-stability]], and let $K\\subset U$ be a compact positive tube. Let $y:[0,T]\\to U$ solve the finite conservative PDS [[def-finite-conservative-production-destruction-system]], set $y_0=y(0)$, and compute each step with [[alg-mprk22-1]]. Suppose the exact solution, all numerical states, and every MPRK22(1) stage remain in the common compact tube $K$, and $h\\le h_0$ for the local constants in that lemma. Then a constant $C_T$, independent of $N$, satisfies\n\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}\\|y_n-y(t_n)\\|_2\\le C_T h^2.$$\n\nThis is a fixed-time, compact-tube convergence result; it does not assert a uniform error constant as the tube approaches a zero denominator or as stiffness parameters vary.\n\n"
      }
    ]
